{
  "revision": "golden-v2-2026-11-05",
  "notice": "Labels are document-level (a retrieved chunk counts when it comes from the expected source) plus deterministic substring fact checks written by reading the corpus. Splits are structural (dev/calibration/test), not blind: the same author wrote every label in one pass, so test-split numbers are diagnostic, not an unbiased generalisation estimate.",
  "corpusNote": "14 synthetic documents, invented for this project. Nothing here is real policy.",
